# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Holy Maiden · Corinna
# A short story about silence and faith
#
# English translation of ../corinna (examples/corinna).
# Same blocks, same scenes, same timing -- only the words differ.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

:: prologue
@scene cathedral
@play bgm sorrow

@say "A nun of the cathedral — claiming to be a holy maiden, scorning the royal house, spreading heresy—"
@say Magistrate "To the dungeons. Trial tomorrow."
@wait 0.5

@say "He holds up the king's writ, his face empty."
@say "His eyes are iron hooks, and they catch on the maiden's resistance."
@wait 1.0

@say "……"
@wait 0.5

@say "The maiden closes her eyes. Both hands grip the cross in prayer."
@wait 0.5

@play se bell
@say "The guard wrenches her hands behind her. Her knuckles crack."
@say "Fresh blood stays on the cross."
@wait 1.0

@say Magistrate "A nun of the cathedral — no. A witch. Questioned at the tribunal tomorrow."
@say "The magistrate does not look back. He walks to the palace, each step planted."
@jump crowd_voice

:: crowd_voice
@say Crowd "She is no witch — she is a holy maiden! She is the one who brought the rain from God!"
@say Guard "Holy maiden? She is a criminal."
@say "The guard snorts and pulls the maiden on toward the dungeons."
@wait 0.5

@show corinna at 0.394 0.145 0.211 0.75
@say Maiden "Thank you. Truly. The Lord will keep me. Do not be afraid."
@say "The maiden looks at the crowd who spoke for her, and smiles."
@say "Inside her sleeve, her other hand is pinching her own thigh."
@hide corinna
@wait 1.0
@jump cart

:: cart
@fade to 0.0 0.5
@scene street
@fade to 1.0 0.5

@say "The cart's wheels turn slowly forward."
@say "The maiden sees a mother hiding at the roadside with her child."
@say "Days ago she had stood in front of them. Their lips were trembling the same way then."
@wait 0.5
@say "She grips the cross again and prays for them."
@wait 1.0

@play se bell
@say "Clang."
@say "The iron door closes."
@jump cell_night

:: cell_night
@fade to 0.0 0.5
@scene cell
@fade to 1.0 0.5

@say "She drops to her knees at once. Eyes shut. Hands on her knees."
@say "The cross gives off a dim light in the air."
@wait 1.0

@say Maiden "My Lord."
@say "The maiden draws a long breath in. And lets it out."
@wait 0.5
@say Maiden "I am afraid I can serve you no longer."
@wait 1.5

@say "Breathing in the scent of the cross, she hears God whisper at her ear."
@wait 0.5
@say "My believer. This is the sin you were always going to bear."
@wait 1.0

@say "The maiden's brow tightens."
@wait 1.5
@jump trial_eve

:: trial_eve
@fade to 0.0 1.0
@fade to 1.0 0.5

@say Guard "Hey. Holy maiden, whatever you are. Wake up. You cannot be late to your own trial."
@say "The maiden watches the guard unlock the cell."
@say "She follows close behind him."
@wait 0.5
@say "She is pushed into the cart."
@jump trial_outside

:: trial_outside
@fade to 0.0 0.5
@scene court_outside
@fade to 1.0 0.5

@say "She meets the eyes of yesterday's mother. Her lips start to shake."
@wait 1.0
@say "The wheels stop turning."
@wait 0.5
@say "She sees the crowd who spoke for her yesterday, standing in front of the tribunal."
@wait 0.5

@say Crowd "She is not a witch! You devils!"
@say "She sees the sunlight in their hair."
@wait 0.5

@say Magistrate "Get out of the way."
@say "The magistrate strolls over with a pack of guards behind him."
@say "Every one of the crowd tightens their fists."
@say "The guards fan out on either side of the magistrate."
@wait 1.0

@say Maiden "My lord magistrate. Let them go."
@say "The maiden looks at the magistrate and bows her head."
@wait 0.5

@say Magistrate "The dungeons are still mostly empty—"
@say "The magistrate pats his leather cape. His face does not move."
@wait 0.5
@say Magistrate "Would you like to try them?"
@wait 1.5

@say "The sunlight suddenly turns yellow, then black."
@play se gavel
@say "And then a gavel falls."
@fade to 0.0 0.3
@jump trial

:: trial
@scene court
@fade to 1.0 0.5

@say "She just stands there. Watching."
@wait 1.0

@say Clerk "Corinna."
@say "The clerk opens the file and speaks without hurry."
@say Clerk "Do you admit your guilt?"
@wait 0.5

@say "He lists her crimes, word by word, nailing the cross into her palm."
@wait 1.5

@say Corinna "I am guilty."
@wait 1.5

@say "The court goes quiet."
@wait 1.0

@say "She tears the cross off."
@play se bell
@say "It lands on the flagstones with a small sound."
@wait 1.0

@say Judge "Accept your sin, then. Openly."
@say "This is the judge's final ruling."
@wait 2.0
@jump ending

:: ending
@fade to 0.0 1.5
@scene cell_night
@stop bgm
@play bgm sorrow
@fade to 1.0 1.5

@say "Corinna sits on the moldy straw of her cell, eyes on the bright moon in the window."
@wait 1.0
@say "The moonlight sits quietly inside the bars."
@wait 0.5
@say "She crouches down slowly and touches the moon on the floor."
@wait 0.5
@say "Cold. Like her cross."
@wait 1.0

@say "Tears leave her eyes and fall on the back of her hand."
@say "Her cross. The old priest gave it to her."
@wait 0.5
@say "It is gone now."
@wait 1.5

@say "She draws her hand back."
@say "Both knees go down."
@say "Her hands clasp tight. Eyes on the moon. Her lips keep moving."
@wait 2.0

@fade to 0.0 3.0
@say "— The End —"
@quit
